# VPN_SWITCH_GROUP_openvpn - Privilege-drop group for OpenVPN configs
#
# Optional group name enforced in patched OpenVPN configs via the
# "group" directive. Companion to VPN_SWITCH_USER_openvpn.
#
# Default: (empty - "group" directives in configs are left unchanged)
#
# If set, vpn-switch patches configs at connect time:
#   - Existing "group" directives are rewritten to this value
#   - If no "group" directive exists, one is appended
#
# Example:
#   openvpn
#
# Background:
#   The FreeBSD openvpn port >= 2.7 ships a dedicated "openvpn"
#   user/group and recommends migrating configs away from "nobody".
